const intro = `<p>This page answers the questions an engineer, an investor or a policy reader tends to ask on first meeting the Reality Code Engine (RCE), a programming language with a written specification, and RCE-JEPA, a research proposal built on it. It is written to be read top to bottom: each term is defined before it is used, and each number is cited to a paper on this site or to an outside source in the list at the end, numbered in order of first citation.</p>
<p><strong>Status, 22 November 2026, at openIE-dev/rce main <code>1762fb4b</code> (20 November 2026).</strong> Research, in draft. The language, its reference checker, its emitters, its host runtime and its proofs are public code, and every commit of main that passes continuous integration is released as binaries and a container image [[repo]]. The lift of programs from other languages has a first lifter, for a subset of Python, and a probe for one Go pattern [[repo]]. A memory-mapped Gear-0 lookup store, a first compact purpose-trained latent Form joint embedding predictive architecture (JEPA) repair proposer (<code>FormJEPA-v1</code>, <code>8.42M</code> trainable parameters), and the 151-task <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> promotion criterion have now been benchmarked, while full intent-to-Form synthesis and calibrated multi-term energy ranking remain open [[jepa]]. First operating-system and on-chip counter readings (<code>reported_j</code>) now exist on Apple silicon and Linux processor energy counters for <code>rce check</code>, the 62-Form suite, version-control admission, local 35B model repair, and <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> inference, whereas external wall-meter or shunt-rail readings remain empty (<code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>) [[rce,receipts]].</p>`;

